# Minimized reproducers of what the language-server fuzzer
# (scripts/lib/lspfuzz.py, scripts/check-fuzz.sh section 7) found.
# Tab-separated:
#
#   file  status  stage  signature  what
#
# status    `fixed`: section 7 replays the session and it must now pass
#           every oracle (no signal, no hang, well-formed frames and
#           JSON-RPC, every request answered, the right exit status) - a
#           regression test. `open`: it must still fail, at `stage`, with
#           the oracle's reason matching `signature` (an extended regex);
#           an open row that stops failing, or fails differently, turns
#           the gate red.
# stage     signal | hang | frame | jsonrpc | answer | exit (`-` for a
#           fixed row).
#
# A `.lspfuzz` file is the session itself, JSON Lines, with the tree
# named `@ROOT@` so it replays on any host; `lspfuzz.py run --transcript`
# prints what it sends and what comes back.
empty-body.lspfuzz	fixed	-	-	a frame whose body is empty (`Content-Length: 0`) ended the session: `rpcRead` answered "" for it and for the end of the stream alike, so the server read it as the client hanging up and exited 1 with every request behind it unanswered. `rpcReadMsg` answers `Some ""` for the frame and `None` for the end (fixed in stdlib/Rpc.ax, self_host/lsp.ax)
lint-dag.lspfuzz	fixed	-	-	a 219-byte document hung the server for good: a macro that uses its parameter twice, nested 40 deep, expands to a DAG with 2^40 paths, and the editor-only lints walked the EXPANDED tree - `expandProgram` rewrites `decls` in place - on every publish and every code action, though `lspLintDoc` promised the written one. The lints now run over the written tree, taken before expansion (fixed in self_host/lsp.ax `lspCheckDoc`, `lspCodeAction`)
